7. Revised PhD Thesis Structure

7.1 Scope Discipline

The PhD thesis must make one core contribution: a theoretical and empirical account of how certification can function as a coordination mechanism in domains lacking sovereign authority, with application to space infrastructure.

This contribution has three components:

1. Theoretical: Formal model of certification-as-screening in anarchic domains, with scope conditions and testable predictions
2. Comparative: Analysis of how certification institutions emerged in aviation, maritime, nuclear, and other domains, identifying transferable design principles
3. Empirical: Agent-based simulation, stakeholder survey, and case study analysis testing the theoretical predictions

