Appendix D: Stakeholder Interview Protocol

D.1 Interview Design

D.1.1 Objectives

The interviews aim to:

1. Identify certification needs and gaps in the space domain
2. Estimate willingness-to-pay for certification services
3. Understand institutional preferences
4. Assess feasibility of voluntary certification

D.1.2 Sample

Target: 30–50 structured interviews

Participant categories:

· Space agency representatives (10)
· Commercial operators (10)
· Regulatory body representatives (5)
· Insurance underwriters (5)
· Research institutions (10)

D.1.3 Sampling Strategy

Purposive sampling to ensure representation across stakeholder categories. Snowball sampling within categories to identify additional participants.

D.2 Interview Guide

D.2.1 Structured Questions

Section 1: Background

1. What is your role in the space sector?
2. What types of space activities are you involved in?
3. What certification or verification processes do you currently use?

Section 2: Certification Needs

4. What coordination challenges have you experienced in space activities?
5. What information about other actors' systems would help you coordinate?
6. What certification functions are currently missing?

Section 3: Willingness-to-Pay

7. Would you pay for certification of [specific function]? If so, how much?
8. What benefits would certification need to provide to justify the cost?
9. What certification attributes matter most (accuracy, independence, cost)?

Section 4: Institutional Preferences

10. Would you prefer certification by an existing body or a new institution?
11. What governance structure would you trust?
12. What safeguards against capture are essential?

Section 5: Feasibility

13. Do you think voluntary certification is feasible for space activities?
14. What barriers to adoption do you foresee?
15. What would enable certification adoption in your organization?

D.3 Analysis

D.3.1 Coding

Interview responses will be coded using thematic analysis. Codes will be developed inductively from the data and refined through iterative analysis.

D.3.2 Willingness-to-Pay Estimation

For each certification function, the distribution of willingness-to-pay will be estimated from interview responses. This will inform the $B$ parameter in the formal model.

D.3.3 Conjoint Analysis

A subset of interviews will include a conjoint exercise where participants choose between certification scenarios with varying attributes. This enables estimation of attribute weights and willingness-to-pay.

D.4 Ethical Considerations

· Informed consent will be obtained from all participants
· Responses will be anonymized
· Data will be stored securely
· Participants may withdraw at any time

